# Continuous Traceability Assurance (CTA)

Also called the **Gherkin Digital Thread**: a Gherkin-based digital thread connecting
requirements, acceptance criteria, source code, tests, Git revisions, and verification
evidence — then continuously reporting coverage gaps, confirmed failures, evidence that needs
reverification after a change, and unreviewed semantic link suggestions.

Nothing about normal development or testing requires a GPU, LLM, embedding service, vector
database, or network access. The whole project runs from committed fixture data. CocoIndex and
local EmbeddingGemma 2 inference are optional, explicit plugins; live model tests are opt-in.

## Status

**M0, M1, and the expanded M2 engineering gates are satisfied.** M0 was approved at `bca69cf`;
M1 was approved at `e1497cf`; expanded M2 was approved at review 7 and merged via PR #64
(`de4f37a`). The M3 slices AI-06, AI-07, AI-08, and AI-09 are independently approved and merged.

**M3 close-out is implemented locally but not yet accepted or merged.** AS-06 (#28), AS-07 (#29),
AI-03 (#32), and AI-02 (#31) have approved specifications, implementation, offline tests, and
canonical Cucumber execution in the working tree. Independent acceptance reviews, the M3 milestone
review, a PR, and hosted CI are still required. CI-01 (#36) and CI-02 (#37), the M4 automation
stories, have not started.

The current milestone state, evidence, and remaining gates are recorded in
[`docs/STATUS.md`](docs/STATUS.md). The close-out design decisions are in
[`docs/adr/0012-closeout-scope-decisions.md`](docs/adr/0012-closeout-scope-decisions.md).

## Quickstart

```bash
uv sync --project backend
uv run --project backend pytest backend/tests
uv run --project backend uvicorn app.main:app --reload   # http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs
```

That is the whole backend setup. No services, no models, no GPU. `uv sync` needs a package index
once; everything afterwards is offline.

For the dashboard:

```bash
npm ci --prefix frontend
npm run build --prefix frontend
npm test --prefix frontend
```

For the executable acceptance suite:

```bash
npm ci --prefix bdd
(cd bdd && npm run bdd)
node bdd/tools/step-resolution.mjs bdd/reports/cucumber-messages.ndjson
```

## What works today

| Capability | Endpoint / command |
| --- | --- |
| Artifact inventory and one artifact at a baseline | `GET /api/artifacts`, `GET /api/artifacts/{id}?baseline=…` |
| Digital thread: accepted links, proposals separate, evidence | `GET /api/threads/{id}?baseline=…` |
| Deterministic assurance findings over the ingested revision | `GET /api/findings?baseline=…`, `POST /api/assurance/evaluate` |
| Ingestion of the configured fixture repository at a revision | `POST /api/ingestion/run` |
| Discovery proposals from the default fixture provider | `POST /api/discovery` |
| Provider catalogue and typed provider failures | `GET /api/discovery/providers` |
| Capture a discovery candidate as a proposed link | `POST /api/link-proposals` |
| Append-only accept/reject decisions with operator, time, reason, and snapshot hashes | `POST /api/links/{link_id}/review` |
| Review workspace projection and audit history | `GET /api/workspace/threads/{id}`, `/api/workspace/proposals`, `/api/workspace/history` |
| Trusted-local-operator review configuration | `GET /api/review/config` |
| CTA-owned retrieval manifests and refresh planning | `POST /api/retrieval/refresh`, `GET /api/retrieval/manifests[/{baseline}]` |
| Snapshot-bound candidate combination | `POST /api/retrieval/combine` |
| Code retrieval proposals from lexical or CocoIndex-backed search | `POST /api/retrieval/code` |
| Evidence-grounded requirement answers over accepted links | `POST /api/answers` |
| Portable, read-only Gherkin repository indexing and queries | `python -m app.cli index/scenarios/…`; `/api/repositories/*` |
| Reproducible fixture Git history with `baseline-a` / `baseline-b` | `python tools/fixturectl.py all` |
| Offline backend tests, Cucumber acceptance, and the strict step gate | `pytest backend/tests`; `bdd/npm run bdd`; `node bdd/tools/step-resolution.mjs …` |

`POST /api/links/{link_id}/review` is implemented; it no longer returns the M0 `501` contract
response. Acceptance changes review state and the workspace projection only — it never changes
verification status, evidence, findings, baseline reads, or fixture bytes. The review journal is
application-owned, append-only, and must live outside the fixture/evaluated repository.

### Optional local inference (AI-02)

The default discovery provider is `fake`. To use the same-machine EmbeddingGemma 2 provider:

```bash
uv sync --project backend --extra local-embedding
export CTA_LOCAL_EMBEDDING=1
export CTA_LOCAL_EMBEDDING_MODEL_DIR="$HOME/.local/share/cta/models/embeddinggemma-2-text-270m-onnx"
uv run --project backend uvicorn app.main:app
  not `404`.
* The journal is application-owned NDJSON outside the fixture/evaluated repository. A committed
  event is a payload line (with `record_digest`) followed by a matching `{"commit": ...}` line;
  replay accepts only committed pairs. A confirmed rollback yields `durability: "not_committed"`;
  an unconfirmed rollback or a persistent uncommitted tail blocks further mutations with
  `durability: "indeterminate"` / `review-storage-unavailable`.
* Review writes are loopback-only; a missing `Origin` is allowed for local CLI clients, and any
  present Origin must be an `http(s)` loopback origin.

## Provider availability and catalogue (schema 0.7.0, additive; AS-07)

`ProviderDescriptor = {name, kind: "fixture" | "model" | "unknown", default}` and
`ProviderCatalogResponse = {schema_version, default, providers}` describe the **effective** registry.
Presentation kind comes from the versioned `PROVIDER_KINDS` table (`fake` fixture,
`cocoindex`/`local-embeddinggemma` model), not from the provider name; disabling a provider does
not erase the meaning of historical provenance. Problem documents may carry `failed_provider` and
`registered_providers`; both are required on `provider-not-registered`. A registered provider that
fails maps to `503 provider-unavailable` and is never converted into a finding, an accepted link, or
an empty success. Empty discovery success keeps provider/model/index provenance.

## Local embedding provider (schema 0.7.0, additive provider; AI-02)

`local-embeddinggemma` is an optional `CandidateDiscovery` implementation behind the existing port;
the default remains `fake`. It loads the Apache-2.0 EmbeddingGemma 2 text ONNX model from a local
directory, embeds the eligible corpus in memory, and returns ordinary `TraceCandidate` proposals.
The exact model, weights digests, runtime, licence, hardware, formatting versions, measured limits,
and failure modes are recorded in
`docs/reports/omp-closeout/AI-02-MODEL-MANIFEST.md`. A remote endpoint is `400 invalid-request`
before any connection; missing weights, a digest mismatch, a missing runtime, or a non-finite/wrong
dimension/zero embedding are `503 retrieval-unavailable`. The provider writes no accepted link,
review state, evidence, or finding.

## Retrieval lifecycle contracts (schema 0.8.0, additive; AI-03)

The CTA-owned snapshot/cache lifecycle lives in `app/domain/retrieval_lifecycle.py` and
`app/retrieval/lifecycle.py`; the normative notes are in `docs/stories/AI-03.md`.

* `RetrievalConfig` — provider, model ID/version, weights digest, runtime, formatting version,
  dimension, max tokens, and explicit `chunking_owner`/`embedding_owner = cocoindex`.
  `config_digest = sha256(canonical config)`.
* `RetrievalArtifact` — eligible `CODE-nnn`/`TEST-nnn` artifact ID, type, locator, revision, and
  content hash.
* `ContentChangePlan` — `changed`, `added`, `removed`, and `unchanged` artifact IDs plus the
  resolved selected/previous commits. It has no embedding-count field.
* `RetrievalManifest` — schema version, repository, baseline, commit, config/config digest,
  `corpus_cache_key`, `snapshot_binding`, eligible artifacts, change classifications and counts,
  `items_embedded` (nullable), `items_embedded_availability` (`measured` | `not_available`),
  measured `elapsed_ms`, previous binding, `reused`, `published_at`, and the optional backend
  observation.
* `corpus_cache_key = sha256(repository, config_digest, sorted eligible artifact IDs/types/locators/
  content hashes)`; commits are excluded. `snapshot_binding = snapshot:sha256(sha256(repository,

## Discovery

### `POST /api/discovery`

Request:

```json
{ "artifact_id": "SCN-001", "top_k": 5, "relation_types": null, "provider": null, "baseline": "baseline-a" }
```

* `top_k` 1…50 (default 5); `relation_types` restricts proposals; `provider` overrides the
  configured default (`CTA_DISCOVERY_PROVIDER`, default `fake`); `baseline` binds the request to a
  tag or commit SHA.
* A registered provider that cannot execute returns `503 provider-unavailable` with
  `failed_provider`; the application never falls back to `fake`. A valid empty result is `200` with
  `candidates: []` and retained provider/model/index provenance. Provider failure never becomes a
  finding.

Response (abridged; `fixtures/api-responses/discovery.SCN-001.json` is the full sample):

```json
{
  "schema_version": "0.7.0",
  "artifact_id": "SCN-001",
  "provider": "fake",
  "model_version": "fake-fixture-v1",
  "index_revision": "sha256:acb64531ff9e59bdad1de5f61232eff7cb2e4528de28da9bb25c85b58278da3d",
  "candidates": [
    {
      "source_id": "SCN-001",
      "target_id": "CODE-001",
      "proposed_relation_type": "implemented_by",
      "rank": 1,
      "score": 0.94,
      "discovery_provider": "fake",
      "model_version": "fake-fixture-v1",
      "index_revision": "sha256:acb64531ff9e59bdad1de5f61232eff7cb2e4528de28da9bb25c85b58278da3d",
      "rationale": "The scenario steps match Account.withdraw in src/accounts.py."
    }
  ]
}
```

Guarantees, asserted by tests: candidates carry no `link_id` and no `review_state`; no accepted
link or evidence record is created or modified; a known artifact with no proposals returns an
empty list; unknown artifact → 404 `artifact-not-found`; unknown provider → 400
`provider-not-registered` with `failed_provider` and `registered_providers`; provider failure →
503 `provider-unavailable`; no automatic fallback.

### `GET /api/discovery/providers`

Returns the effective registry with presentation kind:

```json
{
  "schema_version": "0.7.0",
  "default": "fake",
  "providers": [
    {"name": "fake", "kind": "fixture", "default": true},
    {"name": "cocoindex", "kind": "model", "default": false}
  ]
}
```

`kind` comes from the versioned provider-kind table, not from the provider name. Optional providers
absent from the effective registry are not listed; historical proposals retain their recorded
provenance and are labelled from the static table.

### Local embedding provider (AI-02, additive)

When `CTA_LOCAL_EMBEDDING=1` and a local model directory is installed, the effective registry also
lists `local-embeddinggemma` (`kind: model`). It implements the same request/response contract; a
remote endpoint is `400 invalid-request` before any connection, and missing weights or malformed
embeddings are `503 retrieval-unavailable`. The exact manifest is in
`docs/reports/omp-closeout/AI-02-MODEL-MANIFEST.md`.
class ScenarioNotFound(DomainError):
    """A portable query named a scenario key that does not exist at the pinned revision."""

    code = "scenario-not-found"
    title = "Scenario not found"
    status = 404


class RetrievalUnavailable(DomainError):
    """A configured optional retrieval provider could not be used."""

    code = "retrieval-unavailable"
    title = "Retrieval unavailable"
    status = 503


class RetrievalSnapshotNotFound(DomainError):
    """No retrieval manifest is published for the requested baseline or binding."""

"""Optional CocoIndex Code search adapter (workstream A).

CocoIndex Code is an external, rebuildable *code-search cache*. This module is deliberately not a
:class:`app.domain.ports.CandidateDiscovery`: it has no artifact repository, no link vocabulary, no
review state, and no evidence writer. It turns one structured MCP ``search`` response into
non-authoritative hits that a later slice (AI-06 PR 2) may map to ``TraceCandidate`` values.

The default application never imports the live transport and never starts ``ccc``. Only
:class:`app.discovery.cocoindex_mcp.StdioMcpTransport` spawns a process, and only when a caller has
configured an explicit project root and live opt-in.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

import json
import math
import time
from collections.abc import Callable, Mapping, Sequence
from dataclasses import dataclass
from pathlib import Path, PurePosixPath
from typing import Any, Protocol, runtime_checkable

from pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict, Field, ValidationError, field_validator

COCOINDEX_PROVIDER = "cocoindex-code"
DEFAULT_LIMIT = 5
MAX_LIMIT = 100
MAX_QUERY_CHARS = 2_000
MAX_FILTERS = 10
MAX_FILTER_CHARS = 200
MAX_PATH_CHARS = 1_024
MAX_LANGUAGE_CHARS = 64
MAX_RESPONSE_BYTES = 512 * 1_024
MAX_HIT_CONTENT_CHARS = 256 * 1_024
MAX_REPORTED_MESSAGE_CHARS = 500

#: The only server identity this adapter is tested against. A different version is a capability
#: error until it is reviewed and added here; see ADR 0008.
SUPPORTED_SERVER_NAME = "cocoindex-code"
SUPPORTED_SERVER_VERSIONS = frozenset({"0.2.43"})


class CocoIndexError(Exception):
    """Typed adapter failure. Details contain no credentials or process environment values."""

    code = "cocoindex-error"

    def __init__(self, detail: str) -> None:
        self.detail = detail
        super().__init__(detail)

    def __str__(self) -> str:
        return f"{self.code}: {self.detail}"


class CocoIndexConfigurationError(CocoIndexError):
    """The executable, project root, or project marker is missing or unsafe."""

    code = "cocoindex-configuration-error"


class CocoIndexRequestError(CocoIndexError):
    """A bounded request field was rejected before any process started."""

    code = "cocoindex-request-error"


class CocoIndexUnavailableError(CocoIndexError):
    """The server could not be started, exited early, or closed its pipes."""

    code = "cocoindex-unavailable"


class CocoIndexTimeoutError(CocoIndexError):
    """The total deadline expired; the process the adapter started was reaped."""

    code = "cocoindex-timeout"


class CocoIndexProtocolError(CocoIndexError):
    """A malformed or incompatible MCP response or search payload was rejected whole."""

    code = "cocoindex-protocol-error"


class CocoIndexQueryError(CocoIndexError):
    """The server reported ``success=false`` or an MCP tool error; no hits are returned."""

    code = "cocoindex-query-error"


class CocoIndexCapabilityError(CocoIndexError):
    """The server name, version, or tool schema is not the reviewed contract."""

    code = "cocoindex-capability-error"


def _clean_text(value: str, *, field: str) -> str:
    if not value or not value.strip():
        raise CocoIndexRequestError(f"{field} must be non-empty")
    if len(value) > MAX_QUERY_CHARS:
        raise CocoIndexRequestError(f"{field} must be at most {MAX_QUERY_CHARS} characters")
    if "\x00" in value:
        raise CocoIndexRequestError(f"{field} must not contain NUL")
    return value


def validate_relative_path(value: str, *, field: str) -> str:
    """Require a normalized, relative POSIX path.

    A returned hit path and a request path filter share this rule. Literal paths are valid globs
    (a pattern with no wildcard matches itself); the point is to keep the selector inside the
    configured project rather than to demand wildcards.
    """
    if not isinstance(value, str) or not value:
        raise ValueError(f"{field} must be a non-empty string")
    if len(value) > MAX_PATH_CHARS:
        raise ValueError(f"{field} must be at most {MAX_PATH_CHARS} characters")
    if "\x00" in value:
        raise ValueError(f"{field} must not contain NUL")
    if "\\" in value:
        raise ValueError(f"{field} must use POSIX '/' separators")
    if value.startswith("/") or value.startswith("//"):
        raise ValueError(f"{field} must be relative, not absolute")
    if len(value) >= 2 and value[1] == ":" and value[0].isalpha():
        raise ValueError(f"{field} must not carry a drive prefix")
    parts = value.split("/")
    if any(part in {"", ".", ".."} for part in parts):
        raise ValueError(f"{field} must not contain empty, '.' or '..' components")
    if str(PurePosixPath(value)) != value:
        raise ValueError(f"{field} must be a normalized path")
    return value


class CocoIndexSearchRequest(BaseModel):
    """A bounded search request. ``refresh_index`` defaults to false: no implicit index mutation."""

    model_config = ConfigDict(extra="forbid", frozen=True)

    query: str = Field(min_length=1, max_length=MAX_QUERY_CHARS)
    limit: int = Field(default=DEFAULT_LIMIT, ge=1, le=MAX_LIMIT)
    offset: int = Field(default=0, ge=0)
    refresh_index: bool = False
    languages: tuple[str, ...] = ()
    paths: tuple[str, ...] = ()

    @field_validator("query")
    @classmethod
    def _query(cls, value: str) -> str:
        return _clean_text(value, field="query")

    @field_validator("languages")
    @classmethod
    def _languages(cls, value: tuple[str, ...]) -> tuple[str, ...]:
        if len(value) > MAX_FILTERS:
            raise ValueError(f"at most {MAX_FILTERS} language filters are allowed")
        for language in value:
            if not language or len(language) > MAX_LANGUAGE_CHARS:
                raise ValueError(
                    f"language filters must be 1..{MAX_LANGUAGE_CHARS} characters each"

