    26	### Problem extensions
    27	
    28	`ProblemDetails` gains two optional extension members:
    29	
    30	|Member|Type|Presence|
    31	|---|---|---|
    32	|`failed_provider`|string|Required on `provider-not-registered`; present when a registered discovery provider cannot execute.|
    33	|`registered_providers`|list[string]|Required on `provider-not-registered`; the effective registry, including enabled optional providers.|
    34	
    35	The extension members are additive to every problem document; existing problem shapes remain valid.
    36	`registered_providers` comes from `ProviderRegistry.registered`, never a hand-maintained copy.
    37	
    38	### Provider outcomes
    39	
    40	|Outcome|HTTP|Code|Body/behaviour|
    41	|---|---|---|---|
    42	|Unknown provider|400|`provider-not-registered`|`failed_provider` = requested name; `registered_providers` = effective list.|
    43	|Registered provider cannot execute|503|`provider-unavailable`|`failed_provider` named; no candidates; no fallback; no finding.|
    44	|Successful empty result|200|—|`DiscoveryResponse` with `candidates: []`, retaining provider/model/index.|
